# Worms of the Earth's "Lands can't enter the battlefield" judges a permanent as it would exist there (CR 614.17d): a Clone
# that chooses to enter as a copy of Dryad Arbor, a land creature, can't enter from the stack and is put into its owner's
# graveyard (CR 608.3e - its example is this one; the card's 2008-08-01 ruling). Bot2 plays Dryad Arbor on turn 2, before
# the Worms is out; on turn 3 Bot1 plays a Swamp, casts the Worms off Black Lotus and Sol Ring, then the Clone off the
# Moxen and the Swamp, copying the Arbor, the only creature.

